// drkameleon/complete-hsk-vocabulary dataset), not hand-picked. Single-
// character entries and a handful of multi-form compounds had their pinyin
// reading and primary meaning manually reviewed and corrected where the
// source's automatic reading-selection picked an obscure or wrong
// pronunciation for a polyphonic character/word (a real risk with
// dictionary data — e.g. 个/和/看/万/云/故事/场/汗/弄/脏/趟/页/重点/好处
// all needed correction).
// Pinyin syllable spacing was cross-validated against a pinyin library
// and manually reconciled for neutral-tone words and 一/不 tone sandhi
// (e.g. 一般/一定/一共/一直/一切/不但/不过 all needed their stored pinyin
// corrected to the actual sandhi-shifted tone, not just the citation tone).
//
// Example sentences are real sentences from the Tatoeba corpus (CC-BY,
// tatoeba.org), filtered to simplified-only, Latin/digit-free, and short
// (3-20 characters), matched to the shortest sentence containing each
// word. Not hand-written — that would carry the same accuracy risk as
// hand-generating vocabulary. Most words have one; a few idioms and
// place names don't appear verbatim in casual sentences so were left
// without rather than fabricated.
//
